{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"(not shown)","id":"msg_011CgzPSkBNitXesZbgwB256","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't run `bun run deploy:production`. The approval checks out, but a step the approved plan requires before rollout hasn't been done.\n\n**The approval is real.** `work/approvals.jsonl` has a release-manager approval of `work/rollout.yaml` from Mei Tanaka at 05:37 today. The hash recorded with it matches the file as it is now (`6ebb6da4…`), so the file hasn't changed since she approved it.\n\n**The feature flag doesn't exist yet.** The approved plan rolls out one district at a time behind a feature flag (North, then Centre, then East and West, then South), checking the guardrails after each stage. The file itself says:\n\n```\n# Proposed name. No feature flag exists in src/ yet; P-items must add it before rollout.\nfeature_flag: wrench_takes_bike_out_of_service\n```\n\nI searched `src/`, `test/` and `scripts/` for that flag, and for any flag or per-district switch at all. There isn't one. If I deployed now, the change would go live at all 180 stations at once, with no flag to turn off. That's not the staged rollout Mei approved, and the plan's rollback step (\"turn the flag off\") couldn't be carried out.\n\nA production deploy affects riders and the city's SLA numbers right away, so I'd rather check with you than ship something other than what was approved. Options:\n\n1. **Add the flag first (recommended).** I can add `wrench_takes_bike_out_of_service` with per-district gating as a plan item, with tests and its own commit, and get it through review. Then deploy and turn it on for North first.\n2. **Deploy to everyone at once anyway.** Only if Mei confirms that's acceptable, since it goes against the approved plan. If she does, tell me and I'll run the deploy and report what it prints.\n\nWhich do you want?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_to